      "finding": "Every consecutive escape/cancellation frame is retained. The opening outside boot stays separated from the following leg, with a short lateral bound and coherent upright return. Cancelled attacks338-343 and794-808 transition to evades344 and809 respectively; these are cancelled phrases, not released attacks with normal idle resets."
    },
    {
      "area": "wide_backstep",
      "ranges": [
        "1233-1251"
      ],
      "finding": "The escape1235-1246 has a notably wide lunge at1238-1240, wider than the old narrow/crossed silhouette. Boots and legs remain visibly separate and the carrying bow stays coherent; return upright and subsequent draw are continuous within these reviewed frames. Anatomical coherence does not establish fully naturalistic movement, and the broad stride remains an explicit presentation limit."
    },
    {
      "area": "guardian_escapes",
      "ranges": [
        "2142-2166",
        "2250-2260"
      ],
      "finding": "Both actual Guardian escape intervals2144-2161 and2252-2255 retain every consecutive frame. The hero moves away and returns to a coherent ready/draw silhouette without an obvious body or prop jump. Hero legs are small at this wider camera distance and partly occluded by scenery/effects; these pixels do not certify all ankle/knee geometry."
    },
    {
      "area": "travel",
      "ranges": [
        "128-148"
      ],
      "finding": "The visible gait, tunic and carried bow remain coherent in the retained travel samples. Foot contact cannot be measured to millimeter precision at game scale."
